  "question": "Let $A = \\begin{bmatrix} 0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}$ and $I$ is the $2 \\times 2$ identity matrix. Which of the following is $A + A^T$?",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "$A^T = \\begin{bmatrix} 0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}$.<br /><br />$A + A^T = \\begin{bmatrix} 0+0 & 2+(-2) \\\\ -2+2 & 0+0 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}$.<br /><br />Thus, $A + A^T = 0$.",
